course: dictionary
lesson: 15226
title: Severity: how serious something is
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Severity is a noun, and it tells you how serious, strong or bad something is. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «The doctor checked the severity of the cut before she put on a bandage.» The doctor needed to know how bad the cut was, so severity means how serious it was.
explain: Severity can also mean strictness. «The head teacher spoke with severity, and nobody dared to giggle.» Nobody giggled because the teacher was stern, so here severity means harshness. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about how bad something is, or how strict someone is?
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The doctor checked how serious the cut was» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Severity is a noun. It is the severity of something.
fact: Severity means how serious, strong or bad something is, such as an illness, an injury or a storm.
fact: Severity can also mean strictness or harshness, as in a teacher's severity.
fact: «Depending on the severity» means the result changes with how serious something is.
fact: «Reduce the severity» means make something less serious, as in «reduce the severity of a cold».
exercise: «The doctor checked the severity of the cut before she put on a bandage.» What does severity mean here? | How many colours the bandage had | The shape of the bandage | How quickly the cut would stop bleeding | *How serious the cut was
exercise: «The head teacher spoke with severity, and nobody dared to giggle.» What does severity mean here? | Speed and quickness | Loud noise | Kindness and joy | *Strictness and harshness
exercise: «The storm had great severity, and it closed the roads for three days.» Find and copy one word that tells you the storm was very bad. | *severity | roads | three | storm
test: «Depending on the severity of the injury, you may need to call for help.» What does depending on the severity mean? | It depends on what colour the injury is | It depends on the day of the week | It depends on how many people are there | *It depends on how serious the injury is
test: «Wearing a coat can reduce the severity of the cold wind.» What does reduce the severity mean? | Make the wind into a song | *Make the wind less serious | Make the wind come closer | Make the wind last longer
exam: The judge spoke with great severity, and the whole court went quiet. What does severity mean here? | *Strictness and harshness | Tiredness after a long day | Speed and noise | Happiness and laughter
